A 2003 paper in the Bulletin of Economic Research

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:40.000
looked at a variety of sports betting markets

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:46.360
where bookmakers set the odds. The bias showed up. The exact shape was not the same from market to

00:06:46.360 --> 00:06:52.700
market. The paper also found evidence for a central shin prediction. Margin's rise as the number

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:59.340
of competitors rises. A bigger field gives an insider more places to hide a bet and gives the bookmaker

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:06.800
more reason to widen the take. A 2002 paper in economica asked whether a sharp shortening of odds is

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:14.300
information or a crowd chasing a crowd. NFR crafts had suggested in 1985 that a pronounced

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:20.400
shortening could signal an insider. Those authors measured insider incidents, the shin measure,

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:26.460
at opening prices and again at starting prices. When odds shortened and that measure rose,

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:31.760
betting returns were significantly positive. When odds shortened and the measure fell,

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:37.040
returns were negative. The authors read that second case as herd behavior, not

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:42.180
information. So a move can be someone who knows something. That pulls the price

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:46.920
